## 6. Verifying

Automated checks, from the workspace root:

```powershell
py -3 -m unittest discover -s extensions/{{ extension }}.extension/tests
```

The server's own tests need the packages from its `requirements.txt` (use the
virtual environment from Step 3):

```powershell
servers\revit-mcp\mcp-server\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest servers\revit-mcp\mcp-server\tests -q
```

For a live check, start a disposable model, apply the reload rule above, then
request `{{ routes_url }}/health/` (for example with `Invoke-RestMethod`).

The foundation's verifier (run from the foundation checkout, not this
workspace) can exercise all five routes and tools and write redacted
evidence:

```powershell
py -3.11 -m formwork_cli verify revit --repository "<workspace>" --routes-url {{ routes_url }} --routes-reset-confirmed
```

`--routes-reset-confirmed` is a human assertion that Revit was restarted, or
Routes toggled off and on, after the most recent pyRevit Reload. The tool
cannot check this and refuses to run without it; it is not a magic safety
incantation. The verifier's MCP half uses the foundation's reference copy of
the server, so it proves the Routes contract of this extension rather than
this workspace's server files.
